    "result_text": "The full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, which is the only test class in the repo) passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `timezone` field to the owner resource, following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions used by `locality` and the other derived fields.\n\nThree changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the owner schema (right after `locality`), documenting that it's the IANA name from the fixed region-to-timezone table. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `timezone` field on build.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the fixed `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a static `timezone(customerCode)` method that derives the region via the existing `locality(...)` method and looks up the IANA name, returning `null` for unmapped regions (e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` and a `formatTimezone(owner)` helper, mirroring `formatLocality`.\n\nBecause timezone is derived from the same `customerCode` REGION segment that `locality` uses, an owner with locality `NSW` (Sydney, postcode 2000) now returns `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`, exactly as the test asserts.",
