    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive mirror of the existing `locality` feature at every layer:\n\n- `Owner.timezone(String)` sits directly after `Owner.locality(String)`, reuses it (`REGION_TIMEZONE.get(locality(customerCode))`) rather than re-deriving the region, and its `REGION_TIMEZONE` table is placed alongside the sibling `CITY_REGION` table \u2014 the natural home for a fixed lookup table in this class.\n- `OwnerMapper.formatTimezone` follows the same shape as the adjacent `formatLocality`/`formatContactPreference` helpers (null guard, delegate to the static `Owner` method) and is placed next to `formatLocality`.\n- The `@Mapping` entry and the OpenAPI `timezone` schema are registered in the same way and in the same grouping as the peer fields.\n\nLogic lives in the right unit (derivation in the model, null/presentation handling in the mapper), nothing is duplicated, and no class or method is turning into a catch-all. A maintainer would find this natural.",
